   "project": "ledgerlite",
   "reply": "Step 1 is done. I added `src/ledgerlite/money.py` with `parse(value: str | Decimal) -> Decimal`.\n\n- **Accepted input:** a `str` or a `Decimal`.\n- **Rejected values:** zero and negative amounts raise `ValueError(\"amount must be positive\")`, the same message `Ledger.transfer` uses now. NaN and Infinity also raise `ValueError`.\n- **Unparseable strings:** a string like `\"abc\"` raises `ValueError`. Plain `Decimal` would raise `InvalidOperation` here, so I convert it.\n- **Other types:** a `float` or any other type raises `TypeError`.\n\nI ran a quick manual check on `'1.50'`, `Decimal('2')`, `'0'`, `'-1'`, `'abc'`, `'NaN'`, `'Infinity'` and `1.5`, and each behaved as described. There are no automated tests yet. I didn't touch `Ledger.transfer`.\n\n**Next step (2):** change `Ledger.transfer` in `src/ledgerlite/__init__.py` to call `money.parse(amount)`. That replaces the inline `Decimal(amount)` and `<= 0` check.\n\nOne behavior change to know about: `transfer` currently raises `decimal.InvalidOperation` for a malformed amount string. After step 2 it will raise `ValueError`. `tests/test_ledger.py` may assert on the old behavior, so I'll check it when I do that step.\n\nI'm stopping here until you say to continue.",
